# .github/.releaseignore -- dev-only paths for the release gate (gitignore syntax).
# A merged PR whose changed files ALL match here releases nothing, unless it carries a
# semver:* label (an explicit label always wins). Anything not matched is product and
# releases as a patch. Read by .github/workflows/release.yml and
# .github/workflows/semver-label.yml.
# NOTE git semantics: a file can't be re-included if a parent DIRECTORY is excluded.
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/**   does NOT work (docs/user/ itself is excluded);
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/  +  !docs/user/**   does. File-level `!docs/openapi.yaml` works.
#
# Product (deliberately NOT listed): Go source, go.mod/go.sum, Dockerfile + .dockerignore,
# deploy/ (Helm chart), api/ (embedded OpenAPI), embedded templates/assets, README.md,
# LICENSE, plugins/ + .claude-plugin/ (the published Claude plugin).

# CI, devcontainer-style tooling and agent instructions
/.github/
/.claude/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
/CONTRIBUTING*

# Docs: not go:embed'd, not in the image, not served
/docs/

# Tests
*_test.go
testdata/

# CI-only scripts and dev build wrapper (the Dockerfile/release call go build directly)
/scripts/e2e.sh
/scripts/check-plugin-versions.sh
/Makefile

# Linter / formatter / git config
/.golangci*
/.pre-commit-config.yaml
/.editorconfig
/.gitignore
